Let $I=(x_-,x_+)$ be a bounded interval, let $u\in H^1_0(I;\mathbb R^N)$ satisfy $$\int_I u(x)u(x)^{\mathsf T}\,dx=I_N,$$ and let $K=\operatorname{diag}(k_1,\ldots,k_N)$ with every $k_i>0$. Suppose $M$ and $\mu$ have the regularity and properties <a href="#path:equivariance" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="path:equivariance">[path:equivariance]</a>–<a href="#path:coordinate" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="path:coordinate">[path:coordinate]</a> just stated. For every $\varepsilon>0$, there are a real lower triangular matrix $C$ and a path $B\in C^1(\overline I;\operatorname{Sym}_N)$ such that, with $a=Cu$, $$\label{path:equation}
 \varepsilon B'=M(B)-aa^{\mathsf T},
 \qquad B(x_-)=K,\qquad B(x_+)=-K.$$ These choices satisfy $$\label{path:operator-bound}
 \|B(x)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\|K\|_{\mathrm{op}}
 \qquad(x\in I).$$ For fixed $M$, $K$, and $I$, the matrices $C$ can be chosen bounded uniformly for $0<\varepsilon\leq1$.

Let $I$ be a bounded interval and $0\leq W\in L^p(I)$. If $-k_1^2,\ldots,-k_N^2$ are the first $N$ negative Dirichlet eigenvalues of $-d^2/dx^2-W$, ordered so that $k_1\geq\cdots\geq k_N>0$, then $$\label{spectral:dirichlet-bound}
 \sum_{j=1}^N k_j^{2\gamma}
 \leq \ell_\sigma\int_I W^p.$$
